  "scope_inspection": {
    "method": "All 17 original screenshots and enlarged measurement strips visually inspected. OCR used only as a cross-check; values transcribed from visible pixels.",
    "measurement_status": "Display readings, not calibrated oscillator ground truth. No paired exact patch, MIDI, effects state or independent measurement uncertainty.",
    "instrument": "Rigol MSO5204",
    "source_text_observations": [
      "The author separately describes changed composite shape after each keypress and slow relative-phase movement while both octave keys remain held.",
      "The held-note observation concerns two notes from the SH-201, not comparison against an external clock or generator.",
      "December follow-up says roughly a dozen/severalteen seconds of holding to notice movement; it does not specify a full phase-cycle period.",
      "Keyboard dynamics were reportedly disabled; no raw fixed velocity is supplied."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Classic oscillator choice, oscillator mixture, fine tuning, master tuning, effects, pitch modulation and per-capture patch settings are unknown.",
      "The frequency counter on a composite or irregular waveform cannot identify individual oscillator frequencies.",
      "Separate capture timestamps and trigger levels prevent deriving continuous phase speed from the images.",
      "Retrigger differences cannot distinguish free-running phase, randomized phase, voice allocation or key timing.",
      "No dry isolated triangle, saw or square capture is identified, so waveform shape and polarity are not calibration targets."
    ],
